Z||000015||StuGood||10-08-2000||05:58 PM||||Well, that mirror looks pretty bad -  I guess there's no looking back now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">...  sorry, I know, it's so funny you forgot to laugh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>I'm just glad whoever did it was man (or woman) enough to take responsibility for what they did and leave a note.  Sounds like they want to make it right with you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.<P>Accidents happen - they just do.  About a month ago, I tapped a big old 4x4 truck while pulling into a parking space.  Was going a fraction of a mile per hour, but it shook the truck. Usually I try to be so careful. Momentary lapse of concentration, and thunk!  <B>Should</B> have thunk about what I was doing, but it was too late.<P>I got out and looked, but the truck was so old and beat up, I couldn't tell if I had contributed any real damage.  So I left a note describing what had happened, along with my phone numbers.  What else could I do at that point?           ||||reg||9
